    "narrative": "The outlook for Ghost Ride the WHIP on 2026-07-26 is anchored by two high-efficiency starts against Miles Mikolas, who projects as a primary target for our speed-oriented strategy. **Corbin Carroll** leads the squad with an elite 85.94 score, benefiting from a +10% order boost and a +4% park factor; his ability to exploit the pitcher\u2019s slow delivery (87% SB success probability) makes him our top priority for stolen bases. **Gabriel Moreno** follows suit with a strong 70.65, bolstered by a +17% SP skill advantage and a favorable #3 slot. Elsewhere, **Austin Riley** (70.38) and **Isaac Paredes** (68.21) offer high-floor production, with **Austin Riley** seeing a massive +16% park boost that outweighs his lower-order placement. **James Wood** remains a locked-in core play, capitalizing on a stellar 67.80 score and an elite 0.423 xwOBA, while **Mickey Moniak** serves as a strategic platoon play, leveraging a +14% platoon advantage against the right-handed Jacob Misiorowski despite a tough SP matchup.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Travis Bazzana**, who narrowly missed the starting cut with a 39.05 score, falling just below our 40-point efficiency floor. While his platoon advantage against Rasmussen offered some upside, his negative park and SP skill adjustments rendered him too high-risk for our current game-cap preservation strategy. We are also monitoring the lineup status of **Dalton Rushing**, **Jose Caballero**, **Edwin Arroyo**, **Brice Turang**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Seiya Suzuki**, and **Josh Naylor**; their current projections assume historical batting order spots, and any downward shift in the order could further suppress their already marginal scores. Managers should be particularly wary of the matchup for **Josh Naylor** against Jacob deGrom, as the -19% SP skill penalty significantly compresses his ceiling. Note that **Trevor Story** and **Giancarlo Stanton** remain unavailable due to IL status, while bench depth players like **Cole Young**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Max Muncy**, **Zach McKinstry**, and **Henry Bolte** remain in reserve should any late lineup scratches necessitate a pivot.",
